        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>NASA's Artemis Mobile Launchers</title>\n  <script>\n    window.MathJax = { tex: { inlineMath: [['$', '$']], displayMath: [['$$', '$$']] } };\n  </script>\n  <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\"></script>\n  <style>\n    * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n    html, body { margin: 0; min-height: 100%; }\n    body {\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n      color: #fff;\n      background:\n        radial-gradient(circle at 63% 78%, rgba(222,59,132,.72) 0, rgba(222,59,132,.18) 23%, transparent 48%),\n        linear-gradient(128deg, #273b8f 0%, #283b91 43%, #842886 100%);\n    }\n    .page {\n      width: 768px;\n      min-height: 1024px;\n      margin: 0 auto;\n      padding: 31px 33px 20px;\n      overflow: hidden;\n      position: relative;\n    }\n    .topline {\n      font-size: 14px;\n      letter-spacing: 8px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      line-height: 1;\n      margin: 1px 0 7px;\n      white-space: nowrap;\n    }\n    .logos {\n      position: absolute;\n      top: 22px;\n      right: 27px;\n      display: flex;\n      align-items: center;\n      gap: 12px;\n      color: white;\n    }\n    .nasa-logo {\n      width: 45px;\n      height: 45px;\n      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.5);\n      border-radius: 50%;\n      font-size: 10px;\n      font-weight: bold;\n      font-style: italic;\n      display: flex;\n      justify-content: center;\n      align-items: center;\n      transform: rotate(-14deg);\n    }\n    .artemis-logo {\n      width: 35px;\n      text-align: center;\n      font-size: 10px;\n      font-weight: bold;\n      border-top: 3px solid #fff;\n      padding-top: 3px;\n    }\n    h1 {\n      font-size: 29px;\n      line-height: 1;\n      margin: 0 0 7px;\n      letter-spacing: -.5px;\n    }\n    .intro {\n      font-size: 9.5px;\n      line-height: 1.12;\n      width: 570px;\n      margin: 0;\n    }\n    .rocket-zone {\n      height: 474px;\n      position: relative;\n      margin-top: 6px;\n    }\n    .rocket-layout {\n      display: grid;\n      grid-template-columns: 218px 218px 1fr;\n      gap: 12px;\n      height: 100%;\n    }\n    .launcher {\n      position: relative;\n      height: 445px;\n      padding-top: 14px;\n    }\n    .height-note {\n      position: absolute;\n      left: 1px;\n      top: 25px;\n      height: 388px;\n      border-left: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.85);\n      font-size: 9px;\n      color: #fff;\n      writing-mode: vertical-rl;\n      transform: rotate(180deg);\n      padding-left: 5px;\n      line-height: 1;\n    }\n    .launch-placeholder {\n      width: 184px;\n      height: 388px;\n      margin-left: 22px;\n      margin-top: 3px;\n      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.3);\n      color: rgba(255,255,255,.8);\n      font-size: 10px;\n      display: flex;\n      align-items: center;\n      justify-content: center;\n      text-align: center;\n      background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(255,255,255,.08), rgba(15,15,44,.1));\n    }\n    .launcher-caption {\n      width: 220px;\n      text-align: center;\n      font-size: 10px;\n      line-height: 1.25;\n      margin-top: 8px;\n    }\n    .yellow { color: #fff323; font-weight: bold; }\n    .callouts {\n      padding-top: 3px;\n      position: relative;\n    }\n    .zoom {\n      width: 141px;\n      height: 141px;\n      border: 1.5px solid white;\n      border-radius: 50%;\n      margin: 0 0 8px 0;\n      display: flex;\n      align-items: center;\n      justify-content: center;\n      color: rgba(255,255,255,.85);\n      text-align: center;\n      font-size: 9px;\n      background: rgba(54,54,132,.28);\n    }\n    .callout-text {\n      position: absolute;\n      left: 150px;\n      width: 95px;\n      font-size: 10px;\n      line-height: 1.15;\n    }\n    .callout-one { top: 25px; }\n    .callout-two { top: 189px; }\n    .callout-three { top: 310px; }\n    .bottom {\n      display: grid;\n      grid-template-columns: 344px 1fr;\n      gap: 17px;\n      margin-top: 2px;\n    }\n    .copy {\n      font-size: 10px;\n      line-height: 1.13;\n    }\n    .copy p { margin: 0 0 8px; }\n    .copy h2 {\n      font-size: 12px;\n      margin: 8px 0 4px;\n      line-height: 1;\n    }\n    .right h2 {\n      font-size: 12px;\n      margin: 0 0 12px;\n      line-height: 1;\n    }\n    .numbers {\n      display: grid;\n      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n      gap: 14px;\n      font-size: 8px;\n      line-height: 1.45;\n      margin: 0 3px 18px;\n    }\n    .numbers strong {\n      display: block;\n      font-size: 9px;\n      margin-bottom: 7px;\n    }\n    .placeholder.photo {\n      width: 342px;\n      height: 288px;\n      border: 1px solid #222;\n      background: linear-gradient(#e7d9d2 0%, #e8ddd7 50%, #88706a 51%, #b08a7c 100%);\n      color: #333;\n      display: flex;\n      justify-content: center;\n      align-items: center;\n      text-align: center;\n      font-size: 11px;\n    }\n    .credit {\n      font-size: 7px;\n      line-height: 1.15;\n      font-style: italic;\n      margin-top: 4px;\n      width: 340px;\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"page\">\n    <div class=\"logos\">\n      <div class=\"nasa-logo\">NASA</div>\n      <div class=\"artemis-logo\">ARTEMIS</div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"topline\">EXPLORATION GROUND SYSTEMS</div>\n    <h1>NASA’s Artemis Mobile Launchers</h1>\n    <p class=\"intro\">\n      NASA's mobile launchers are designed to send the SLS Space Launch System rocket, Orion spacecraft, astronauts, and<br>\n      large payloads to the Moon in a single launch. With the new universal stage adapter and enhanced exploration upper stage<br>\n      on SLS beginning with Artemis IV, NASA's mobile launcher 2 will have 40% more payload to the Moon compared to<br>\n      mobile launcher 1, which launches the SLS Block 1.\n    </p>\n\n    <section class=\"rocket-zone\">\n      <div class=\"rocket-layout\">\n        <div class=\"launcher\">\n          <div class=\"height-note\">Approx. 370 ft.</div>\n          <div class=\"launch-placeholder placeholder\">[Diagram: Mobile Launcher 1 and rocket]</div>\n          <div class=\"launcher-caption\">\n            <span class=\"yellow\">Mobile Launcher 1</span> (SLS Block 1 Crew)<br>\n            <strong>Artemis I – Artemis II – Artemis III</strong>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"launcher\">\n          <div class=\"height-note\">Approx. 390 ft.</div>\n          <div class=\"launch-placeholder placeholder\">[Diagram: Mobile Launcher 2 and rocket]</div>\n          <div class=\"launcher-caption\">\n            <span class=\"yellow\">Mobile Launcher 2</span> (SLS Block 1B Crew)<br>\n            <strong>Artemis IV &amp; Beyond</strong>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"callouts\">\n          <div class=\"zoom placeholder\">[Diagram: crew access arm<br>and Orion service module]</div>\n          <div class=\"zoom placeholder\">[Diagram: SLS universal<br>stage adapter]</div>\n          <div class=\"zoom placeholder\">[Diagram: exploration<br>upper stage]</div>\n\n          <div class=\"callout-text callout-one\">\n            The <span class=\"yellow\">crew access<br>arm and Orion<br>service module</span><br>\n            will provide a<br>located 40 feet<br>higher on mobile<br>launcher 2.\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"callout-text callout-two\">\n            The new <span class=\"yellow\">SLS<br>universal stage<br>adapter</span> provides<br>\n            increased payload<br>capacity.\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"callout-text callout-three\">\n            The more powerful<br><span class=\"yellow\">SLS exploration<br>upper stage</span><br>\n            requires a new<br>umbilical on mobile<br>launcher 2 along<br>with enhanced<br>propellant loading<br>capabilities.\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class=\"bottom\">\n      <div class=\"copy\">\n        <p>\n          Starting with the Artemis IV mission, NASA will use a new mobile launcher\n          to continue the effort to enable humans to live and work on the lunar\n          surface. Mobile launcher 2 will allow the agency to send heavier,\n          increasingly complex missions to the Moon. The enhanced capabilities of\n          the new mobile launcher will support SLS Block 1B configurations. These\n          larger Artemis rockets will provide the power needed to send astronauts\n          and heavy cargo to the Moon.\n        </p>\n\n        <h2>A Bold Mission Calls for Big Rocket</h2>\n        <p>\n          As Artemis missions evolve, so must our ground support equipment. The\n          powerful SLS Block 1B lifts more than double the mass to the Moon in a\n          single launch as compared to current rockets and features a more powerful\n          upper stage that can send both crew and large payloads to space for our\n          most ambitious missions ever attempted. These heavy cargo missions\n          demand a larger and more robust mobile launcher to support SLS\n          launch and withstand the tremendous power of such a large rocket.\n        </p>\n\n        <h2>What’s New with Mobile Launcher 2?</h2>\n        <p>\n          NASA engineers implemented lessons learned from the construction of\n          mobile launcher 1 and the launch of Artemis I to make improvements to\n          the next generation mobile launcher. These improvements will enable\n          mobile launcher 2 to better withstand the immense launch power of SLS\n          Block 1B.\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          Structurally, the new mobile launcher will feature a wider cross-section on\n          the launch tower to better protect equipment and an increased diameter on\n          piping and flow nozzles of the ignition overpressure sound suppression\n          system for a better flow of water into the launch platform and flame hole.\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          New technology includes: a self-contained ground cooling system\n          providing air cooling for Orion, reducing reliance on ground support\n          equipment; an improved electrical system; and a new payload\n          accommodations room enabling customers to remotely communicate with\n          payloads.\n        </p>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"right\">\n        <h2>Mobile Launcher by the Numbers:</h2>\n        <div class=\"numbers\">\n          <div>\n            <strong>Mobile launcher 1</strong>\n            Total height above ground: 380 ft<br>\n            Tower: 40 x 8 square, about 355 ft tall<br>\n            Approximate weight: 10.5 million lbs\n          </div>\n          <div>\n            <strong>Mobile launcher 2</strong>\n            Total height above ground: 402 ft<br>\n            Tower: 40 x 50 ft square, about 377 ft tall<br>\n            Approximate weight: 12.4 million lbs\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"placeholder photo\">[Photo: SLS rocket atop mobile launcher at launch pad]</div>\n        <div class=\"credit\">\n          NASA’s Space Launch System rocket atop mobile launcher 1 on Launch Pad 39B at Kennedy<br>\n          Space Center in Florida, prepares for Artemis I. Photo credit: NASA\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n  </main>\n</body>\n</html>",
